"""Write a reproducible, corpus-specific English analysis report."""
import argparse,json,hashlib
from pathlib import Path
def report(root):
 def load(n):return json.loads((root/(n+'.json')).read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
 q=load('quality-report');p=load('parameters');s=load('sensitivity')
 lines=['# Exploratory co-citation and citation burst analysis','',f"Source: {p['source']}",f"SHA-256: {p['source_sha256']}",'',f"The sample contains {q['records']} citing documents from {min(p['years'])} to {max(p['years'])}. Annual document counts: {dict(zip(p['years'],p['year_document_counts']))}. Export date(s): {', '.join(q['export_dates']) or 'unknown'}.",'','## Data and methods','',f"There are {q['raw_reference_occurrences']} raw cited-reference occurrences, {q['within_document_reference_duplicates']} within-document duplicate(s), and {q['unique_reference_keys']} normalized reference keys. Single unambiguous DOI strings identify references; {q['ambiguous_multi_doi']} multi-DOI keys remain unresolved. Non-DOI strings receive conservative normalization, not fuzzy identity matching. Reference identities have not been externally verified.",'',f"The graph retains the top {p['top_n']} references with at least {p['min_citations']} citing documents and pairs with at least {p['min_pair']} co-citing documents. Its {q['selected_network_nodes']} nodes and {q['network_edges']} edges yield {q['clusters']} Louvain clusters (cosine weights; seed {p['seed']}; modularity {q['modularity']}). Cluster title phrases are candidate labels, not reviewed topic names. Figure edge thinning affects presentation only.",'',f"Burst detection uses annual local citing-document counts, normalized by the annual corpus size, for all {q['eligible_burst_references']} eligible references. WoS global times-cited values are not annual citation histories. The model is a two-state binomial adaptation of Kleinberg, with s={p['s']}, gamma={p['gamma']} and minimum duration={p['min_duration']}. Strength is the emission log-likelihood gain over baseline, not a p-value or a CiteSpace-equivalent score. Minimum duration filters fitted intervals; it is not a constrained-duration refit.",'','## Results and sensitivity','',f"The configured model identifies {q['burst_intervals']} burst intervals. Of these, {q['ongoing_burst_candidates']} touch the final observation year and are exported as frontier candidates requiring reading and validation.",'','| Gamma | Minimum duration | References with bursts |','|---|---|---|']
 lines += [f"| {x['gamma']} | {x['min_duration']} | {x['references_with_bursts']} |" for x in s]
 lines += ['','## Interpretation limits','',f"The observation window spans {len(p['years'])} calendar years. Short windows and incomplete export-year coverage can produce unstable apparent bursts. Intervals touching either boundary are censored. A final-year burst alone does not establish a research frontier. Low modularity indicates weak separation; cluster layouts should not be interpreted as proof of distinct research specialties.",'','The timeline counts distinct sample papers citing each cluster. A paper can contribute to multiple clusters. Its curves link the same cluster across years and do not encode topic migration, causal transitions or citation flows. No full-text review of the cited references was performed by this pipeline.','', '## Outputs','', '- documents.json / documents.csv: all source documents.','- references.json / references.csv: all normalized references with retained variants.','- cocitation-network.json / cocitation.graphml: selected analysis network.','- bursts.json / bursts.csv: intervals, strengths and censoring flags.','- frontier-candidates.json: final-year burst candidates.','- sensitivity.json / parameters.json / quality-report.json: reproducibility and quality.','- figures/: English PNG (450 DPI), SVG and PDF, with display-network.json.','- literature-summary.xlsx (when export module is run): all documents, bursts, clusters, selected references and sensitivity. Full references remain in CSV/JSON.','', '## Method references','', '- [Kleinberg (2002), Bursty and Hierarchical Structure in Streams](https://www.cs.cornell.edu/home/kleinber/bhs.pdf), Section 4.','- [CiteSpace: Co-citations](https://citespace.podia.com/glossary-cocitations).']
 (root/'Analysis-report.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n',encoding='utf-8')
 files=[dict(file=str(f.relative_to(root)),sha256=hashlib.sha256(f.read_bytes()).hexdigest()) for f in sorted(root.rglob('*')) if f.is_file() and f.name!='manifest.json']
 (root/'manifest.json').write_text(json.dumps(files,indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
if __name__=='__main__':
 p=argparse.ArgumentParser();p.add_argument('--output',required=True);a=p.parse_args();report(Path(a.output))
